course: religion-ethics
lesson: 72
title: What happens after we die? What our church teaches
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: At Sunday school Mrs Patel asks what happens when we die, and Ellie says «You go to heaven»; Christians at Ellie's church believe heaven is being with God for ever, with no more pain or tears, and not a place above the clouds that a telescope could find.
explain: The heart of this hope is Easter: Christians believe Jesus died on the cross and rose again on the third day, so on Easter Sunday the church calls «Christ is risen!» and answers «He is risen indeed!», and Ellie's Ukrainian grandma says «Христос воскрес!» («Christ is risen!») and hears «Воістину воскрес!» («Truly he is risen!»).
explain: The vicar explains the creed's words «the resurrection of the body»: Christians believe that at the end of time God will raise the dead to new life with healed bodies that never die, though how is a mystery.
explain: The Bible pictures heaven as a city of gold and a house with many rooms; the clouds and harps of cartoons and old paintings are only pictures, and Christians believe heaven is full life with God, not boredom.
explain: Some questions have no sure answer: whether Grandad can see Ellie, whether Mia's dog will be in heaven; the vicar says «God loves all he has made» and «God knows each heart better than we do», and Christians leave judging to God.
explain: Other faiths and non-religious people see death differently, and in this course every view is treated with respect; this lesson is what Ellie's church teaches.
fact: Christians believe heaven is being with God for ever, where there is no more pain or tears.
fact: Heaven is not a place in the sky that can be seen with a telescope; the Bible describes it with pictures.
fact: Christians believe Jesus died on a cross and rose from the dead on the third day; this is celebrated at Easter.
fact: On Easter Sunday Christians greet each other «Christ is risen!» – «He is risen indeed!»; in Ukrainian «Христос воскрес!» – «Воістину воскрес!».
fact: In the Creed Christians say they believe in «the resurrection of the body and the life everlasting».
fact: Christians believe Jesus died to show God's love and to take away people's wrongdoing so they can be forgiven; churches explain this in different ways.
fact: Christians believe God judges with justice and mercy, and that anyone truly sorry can be forgiven; beliefs about who goes where differ.
fact: Catholic, Orthodox and some Anglican Christians pray for the dead, to show love and ask God to look after them; many Protestants thank God for them instead.
fact: Christians believe people who die stay themselves with God; they do not turn into angels, who are different beings made by God.
fact: «The communion of saints» means that all Christians, living and dead, are joined in God's family.
fact: The Bible does not say clearly whether people in heaven can see what happens on earth.
fact: The Bible says little about animals in heaven; some Christians hope God will make all creation new.
fact: Many Christians believe people will know and love each other in heaven; the Bible says God will «wipe away every tear».
fact: Muslims honour Jesus as a prophet but do not believe he died on the cross; other faiths see Jesus differently.
exercise: What do Christians at Ellie's church believe heaven is? | Being with God for ever, with no more tears | A cloud kingdom that aeroplanes fly past | A place where you can do anything you like | A long sleep where nothing happens
exercise: Can heaven be seen through a telescope? | No; it isn't a place in the sky | Yes, just past the Moon | Yes, on very clear nights | No, only because it is too far away
exercise: What do Christians celebrate at Easter? | Jesus rising from the dead | Jesus being born in Bethlehem | The first harvest of the year | The building of the first church
exercise: On Easter Sunday someone says «Christ is risen!». What is the answer? | «He is risen indeed!» | «And also with you!» | «Happy Easter, everybody!» | «Amen, let us pray!»
exercise: What does Ellie's Ukrainian grandma mean by «Христос воскрес!»? | «Christ is risen!» | «Happy Christmas!» | «God bless you!» | «Peace be with you!»
exercise: What is «the resurrection of the body»? | God raising the dead to new life with healed bodies | Bodies coming out of graves as ghosts at night | Doctors bringing people back with medicine | Souls being born again as animals
exercise: Sam asks if bad people go to heaven. What does the vicar say? | God knows each heart better than we do | Nobody who did wrong can ever be forgiven | Everyone in jail goes straight to hell | Good people get in only if they are rich
exercise: What do Christians believe about people who are truly sorry? | God can forgive them | God never forgives anyone | They must pay money first | Only priests can be forgiven
exercise: Why does Ellie's family pray for Grandad after he has died? | To show love and ask God to look after him | To try to bring him back from the dead to live with them | To find out from him where he hid all of his money | Because he told them to do it, every week, before he died
exercise: Do all Christians pray for the dead? | No; many Protestants thank God for them instead | Yes; every church does exactly the same thing in the same words | No; only Muslims pray for the dead, never Christians | Yes, but only in Latin, and only on the day of the funeral
exercise: What does «the communion of saints» mean? | All Christians, living and dead, joined in God's family | Only famous saints can take communion | Saints share bread with the vicar on Sundays | A special club for people with halos
exercise: Ethan asks why Jesus had to die. What do Christians believe? | To show God's love and take away wrongdoing | Because he lost a battle against the Romans | Because he was old and very ill | Because he wanted to become a ghost
exercise: Can Grandad see Ellie from heaven? | Nobody knows for sure; the Bible doesn't say clearly | Yes, he watches her every minute of the day and every night, from above | No, the dead forget everyone at once | Yes, but only when she is being good
exercise: Mia asks if her dog will be in heaven with Grandad. What does the vicar say? | «God loves all he has made; we can trust him» | «Dogs are not allowed anywhere near heaven» | «Yes, all dogs go to heaven, just like in the film» | «Pets turn into angels when they die»
exercise: Where do pictures of clouds and harps in heaven come from? | Cartoons and old paintings | The exact words of the Bible | Photos taken by astronauts | Reports from people who visited
exercise: Will Ellie recognise Grandad in heaven? | Many Christians believe so, because love does not end | No; everyone in heaven looks exactly the same, like twins | No; people forget each other after death | Yes, because he will look exactly as he did at 80, with his stick and glasses
test: «Heaven's mad boring, you just sit on clouds playing harps innit,» says Freddie's friend in London. What do Christians actually believe? | Heaven is full life with God, joy and love, not boredom | Yes, it's harp lessons for ever and ever, on a cloud, with nothing else to do | Heaven is a long sleep with no dreams | Heaven is a cloud where you wait to be reborn
test: The vicar says, very formally: «We look for the resurrection of the dead, and the life of the world to come.» What is he saying? | Christians hope God will raise the dead to new life | The dead will come back as ghosts on Sunday, to visit their families | Nobody really dies; they just sleep | The world will end next year
test: «Can grandad see me rn? like is he watching?» (rn = right now) asks Ellie. Which answer is honest? | Nobody knows for sure, but love still connects you | Yes, he watches you every second | No, he has forgotten you completely now he's in heaven | Yes, so be good or he'll be cross
test: A boy from Texas says, «My pastor says y'all pray for dead folks, that's sus» (sus = fishy). What's a fair answer? | Churches differ: some pray for the dead, some thank God for them | Every church prays for the dead in the same way | Praying for the dead is against all religions, so the pastor is right to say it's sus | Only Ellie's church has ever done it
test: «If Jesus is God, why'd he have to die? Makes no sense, mate,» says Ethan's uncle in Perth. What's the Christian answer? | To show God's love and take away wrongdoing | He was too weak to stop the Roman soldiers taking him | He did not really die at all; he only fainted | He had to die because he was very old and very ill
test: What would happen to «heaven above the clouds» if you flew past the clouds in a plane? | You'd find only sky; heaven isn't a place in the sky | You'd see the gates of heaven out of the window | You'd be stopped by angels at the border | You'd see the harps but not the people
test: «Will Biscuit be in heaven with Grandad? Ah'd be well chuffed» (chuffed = pleased), says Mia in Leeds. What does the vicar answer? | «God loves all he has made; we can trust him» | «No, animals simply stop when they die, and that is all» | «Yes, all dogs definitely go to heaven, that's a fact» | «Only dogs that went to church with their owners get in»
test: In a cartoon, a grandad dies and becomes an angel with wings. What do Christians teach? | People stay themselves with God; angels are different beings | Every single person who dies becomes an angel with wings and a halo | Only children become angels when they die | Angels are just dead people with wings
test: Sam asks, «Do bad people go to heaven?», and his cousin shouts, «Nah, they go straight to the bad place, end of.» What does the vicar say? | God judges fairly and mercifully; he knows each heart | The cousin is right; it is settled and simple, and nobody can change it | Everyone goes to heaven whatever they do | Nobody can be forgiven after they have died
test: «Christ is risen!» calls the vicar on Easter morning. What is Ellie's grandma's Ukrainian answer? | «Воістину воскрес!» («Truly he is risen!») | «Христос народився!» («Christ is born!») | «Слава Україні!» («Glory to Ukraine!») | «Добрий день, з Великоднем!» («Good day, happy Easter!»)
test: Myth to check: «Christians believe dead people become ghosts who stay in their houses.» | False; Christians believe the dead are with God | True; that is exactly what the Bible teaches about the dead | True, but only for bad people | False, they believe the dead become animals
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the Christian understanding of heaven? | Eternal life in the presence of God, wherein there is neither pain nor sorrow | A physical location situated above the clouds and observable by telescope | A condition of dreamless sleep from which none awakes | A place of idleness in which harps are played without end
exam: Identify the event commemorated by Christians upon Easter Sunday. | The resurrection of Jesus from the dead on the third day | The birth of Jesus at Bethlehem | The descent of the Holy Spirit upon the apostles at Pentecost | The baptism of Jesus in the river Jordan
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning prayer for the departed. | It is practised by Catholic, Orthodox and some Anglican Christians, whereas many Protestants offer thanks instead | It is practised identically by every Christian denomination | It is prohibited by every Christian denomination | It is practised exclusively by the Church of England
exam: Ascertain the signification of the phrase «the communion of saints» as employed in the Creed. | The fellowship of all Christians, both living and departed, in the family of God | A ceremony restricted to persons formally declared saints | The distribution of bread exclusively to clergy | A society of persons who possess miraculous powers
